# RV-Bench local addition (not upstream): fallback flow for cores the
# Surelog/synlig SystemVerilog frontend cannot handle at all.
#
# templates/yosys.j2 reads the sources with `read_systemverilog`, which gives
# the best SystemVerilog coverage but whose failures (Surelog parse errors,
# elaboration errors, UHDM-importer errors) call exit()/abort() rather than
# raising a recoverable TCL error -- so they cannot be caught inside the TCL
# script. YosysFlow.run_tool therefore runs yosys.j2 first and, if that
# process dies, retries with this file, which reads everything through Yosys's
# own Verilog/SystemVerilog frontend. That frontend is more permissive on
# legacy Verilog and on constructs Surelog's parser or importer reject
# (implicit declarations under `default_nettype none`, local declarations in
# unnamed blocks, some system-function uses), and several corpus cores that
# Surelog refuses to parse go straight through `read_verilog -sv`.
#
# Only reached on the failure path, so cores that already synthesise through
# Surelog are untouched.
yosys read_verilog -sv {{ include_dirs_str }} {{ files | join(' ') }}

# RV-Bench local addition (not upstream): mark that the read step
# succeeded, so run_tool() can tell a failed read from a failed
# `-abc9` synth step and only retry the latter with `-noabc9`.
set _rvbench_fh [open "build/rvbench_read_ok" w]
close $_rvbench_fh

# Síntese para ECP5
yosys synth_ecp5 -json {{ output_json }} -top {{ top_module }} {{ synth_ecp5_flags }}
